# Docs AI Layout

## Core file roles

- `docs/ai/WORKFLOW_PROFILE.md` - deploy-time collaboration posture
- `docs/ai/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` - stable project snapshot
- `docs/ai/BOOTSTRAP_DIGEST.md` - short session recovery
- `docs/ai/WORKING_WITH_AI.md` - AI collaboration protocol
- `docs/ai/ACTIVE_WORK.md` - active queue
- `docs/ai/FEATURE_REGISTRY.md` - feature registration
- `docs/ai/PROGRESS_LOG.md` - append-only factual history
- `docs/ai/TECH_DEBT.md` - explicit debt
- `docs/ai/templates/` - reusable doc templates
- `docs/ai/templates/WORKFLOW_PRESETS.md` - preset catalog
- `docs/ai/templates/DOC_GOVERNANCE.md` - gates, complexity levels, Definition of Done
- `docs/ai/templates/DESIGN_PRINCIPLES.md` - structural principle card

## Domain codes

- This repo currently registers **only the `CORE` domain** (framework kernel and shared contracts).
- Further domain codes (`ITEM`, `INVENTORY`, `ABILITY`, `ATTR`, …) are appended to `docs/ai/FEATURE_REGISTRY.md` when the first real requirement for them arrives. Never pre-declare a domain code, and never open an empty domain bucket under `docs/ai/`.

## Naming guidance

- Feature IDs: `DOMAIN-Fnn` (e.g. `CORE-F01`)
- Slice IDs: feature ID plus `-Snn` (e.g. `CORE-F01-S01`)
- Bug IDs: `BUG-DOMAIN-nnn` (e.g. `BUG-CORE-001`)
- ADR IDs: `ADR-` + compact date + sequence (e.g. `ADR-20261026-01`)

### Long-doc filenames (required, ALL CAPS)

```text
docs/ai/DOMAIN/FEATUREID_SLUG_DOCTYPE.md
```

- `DOCTYPE`: `DESIGN` | `IMPLEMENTATION` | `ROADMAP` | `REFACTOR_PLAN`
- Entire filename is ALL CAPS
- The feature-ID segment must match the registry ID (e.g. `CORE-F01_CORE_KERNEL_BOUNDARIES_DESIGN.md`)
- ADR: `ADR-` + compact date + sequence, then `_SLUG.md`
- Bug: `BUG-DOMAIN-nnn_SLUG.md` under `docs/ai/bugs/` or `docs/ai/DOMAIN/bugs/`

## Placement rules

- Design / Implementation / Roadmap / Refactor Plan / ADR docs **must** live under `docs/ai/DOMAIN/` (domain bucket = feature domain, ALL CAPS).
- Do **not** put those long docs in the `docs/ai/` root.
- `docs/ai/` root is reserved for core collaboration truth files only.
- Template examples belong only under `docs/ai/templates/`.
- Session notes are stored in `docs/ai/sessions/` when used.

## Language

- Core collaboration files under `docs/ai/` and these rules are inherited governance and stay in English.
- Project-owned design and implementation docs are written in Chinese; identifiers, code, and quoted API names stay in their original form.
